From 5014872cb2f643a7c043c9d398fb905c5ef54f74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR-Vensuki <260785366+LR-Vensuki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:44:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 32/42] iOS 4-7: Places, Firefox Sync, downloads and shell
 bridges

mobile/ios on MOZ_IOS_LEGACY builds Places and Sync, as desktop does, in
place of GeckoView's app-side history. LegacyFoxPlaces, LegacyFoxSync and
LegacyFoxDownloads give the shell Top Sites, bookmarks, history, the
Mozilla account (WebChannel sign-in) and the download list. Downloads go
through Gecko's helper app service, which uikit left unregistered, with a
plain save-to-disk MIME info.
